The culprit is in the logic that [parses mapping properties](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/f554a6ab2df3a005b9143d53aec650c69dd1c6b7/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/ObjectMapper.java#L257), as a combination of two different stages that occur sequentially: 
1. When a component template is [added](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/6e7bc276222ea39cc655986373e745c9e135bd2f/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/cluster/metadata/MetadataIndexTemplateService.java#L238), its mappings are [parsed](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/f554a6ab2df3a005b9143d53aec650c69dd1c6b7/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/MappingParser.java#L99). When the mapping `properties` section is parsed, the [algorithm](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/f554a6ab2df3a005b9143d53aec650c69dd1c6b7/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/ObjectMapper.java#L316-L333) expands dotted-named fields into parent and sub-fields with intermediate object mapping _if the object is not configured with `subobjects: false`_. When we add a component template that contains a field name like `parent.subfield` and does not contain `subobjects: false`, the parsed mappings will be expanded to:
   ```json
   {
     "_doc": {
       "properties": {
         "parent": {
           "properties": {
             "subfield": {
               "type": "keyword"
             }
           }
         }
       }
     }
   }  

2. Later on, when resolving a composable component template, the formerly parsed mappings is merged with the other component template mappings, which in our case _does_ contain `subobjects: false`. At this point, [another part of the parsing algorithm](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/f554a6ab2df3a005b9143d53aec650c69dd1c6b7/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/ObjectMapper.java#L280-L281) determines the `parent` field's type as `object` because it contains a `properties` entry. This then leads to a [mapping error](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/f554a6ab2df3a005b9143d53aec650c69dd1c6b7/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/ObjectMapper.java#L302) because an object (`parent`) is not allowed to be added to an object  (`_doc`), which at this point is known to be configured with `subobjects: false`.
